@def MICRO_OS_PLUS_MICRO_TEST_PLUS_DEPRECATED_ENABLED
@brief Enables the deprecated definitions of the µTest++ Testing Framework.

@details
This option has no value, only its definition matters.

Without it, the deprecated definitions (the old names of the functions,
the classes, and the members, the overloaded operators, the user-defined
literals, the type wrappers, and the deprecated overloads and
constructors) are neither declared nor defined, so the applications that
still use them fail to compile.

With it, they are available, but marked `[[deprecated]]`, so the
compiler reports their use; the applications that build with `-Werror`
fail until the deprecated definitions are replaced.

The macro must be defined for the library sources too, otherwise the
link of an application that uses the non-inline deprecated members fails
with undefined references.
